Head unit cfg80211 ABI (abi/)
-----------------------------
abi/include/ is the generated header set from Texas Instruments' compat-wireless release
ol_R5.SP8.01, which is what the CMU150's own cfg80211 module was built from. The driver
is compiled against these headers rather than the build kernel's so that struct wiphy,
struct cfg80211_ops and struct station_info match the module already running on the unit.

    https://git.ti.com/git/wl12xx/compat-wireless.git   (tag ol_R5.SP8.01)
    https://git.ti.com/git/wl12xx/compat.git            (tag ol_R5.SP8.01)

These are backported Linux kernel headers plus TI's compatibility layer, GPL-2.0.
abi/Module.symvers is the cfg80211 export list from a build of that tree, trimmed to the
cfg80211 module and rewritten to a relative path. See abi/README.md.

Build kernel
------------
build/Dockerfile downloads Boundary Devices' i.MX6 3.0.35 BSP at a pinned commit into the build
image. It is a compile reference only -- nothing from it is redistributed here or shipped in a
release.

    https://github.com/boundarydevices/linux-imx6   (commit d97f449780544a18ca7c877dfc4742a3d92e4ccf)

